---
/**
 * /blog/babyname-alternative — English "alternative" page for BabyName – find
 * it together (the app with the most ratings in the category), added
 * 2026-11-25 (thread "Ideen aus X-Post prüfen": AI assistants cite
 * "alternative" pages structured like answers).
 *
 * Evidence rule as in apps-en.ts: statements about BabyName come ONLY from
 * its sourced entry (re-read from the US App Store 2026-11-25). Forbidden on
 * this page as everywhere: "BabyName shipped swipe matching in December 2014".
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DisclosureEn from '../../components/DisclosureEn.astro';
import StoreFactsEn from '../../components/StoreFactsEn.astro';
import VsTableEn from '../../components/VsTableEn.astro';
import WhyNamore from '../../components/WhyNamore.astro';
import ClusterFootEn from '../../components/ClusterFootEn.astro';
import Shot from '../../components/Shot.astro';
import { APPS_EN, APP_STORE_EN, PLAY_EN } from '../../data/apps-en';

const rival = APPS_EN.find((a) => a.slug === 'babyname')!;
const canonical = 'https://www.namore.app/blog/babyname-alternative';
const campaign = 'babyname_alternative_en';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is a good alternative to BabyName – find it together?',
    a: 'It depends on what you want to change. For no ads and no account, with a final round that turns your matches into one decision, Namore. For the largest name pool plus a community and an AI assistant, Baby Name Together. For editorial articles about names alongside swiping, Nameberry. All of them let two partners swipe and see the names they both liked.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does BabyName have ads?',
    a: 'Its US App Store listing says “Contains Advertising” and sells a “No Ads $0.99” in-app purchase. Namore shows no ads, including on the free tier.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do couples connect in BabyName and in Namore?',
    a: 'BabyName’s listing describes syncing phones “using a shareable link or AirDrop”. In Namore one partner opens a session and the other joins with a six-letter code; there is no account and no e-mail address.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does BabyName cost compared with Namore?',
    a: 'BabyName’s listing shows several in-app purchases, among them “Epic Parents $7.99”, “Buy all filters $2.99” and “No Ads $0.99”. Namore is free with 100 swipes per partner, then free refills; one single one-time purchase unlocks unlimited swiping and all filters on both phones, priced per country in your app store, with no subscription.',
  },
];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'Article',
      headline: 'Looking for a BabyName alternative?',
      description: 'An alternative to BabyName – find it together for couples: what BabyName’s own listing says, how Namore differs, and which other apps to consider.',
      inLanguage: 'en',
      datePublished: '2026-11-25',
      dateModified: '2026-11-25',
      author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Julian Ziegler' },
      publisher: {
        '@type': 'Organization',
        name: 'Namore',
        logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://www.namore.app/logo@2x.png' },
      },
      mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': canonical },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'FAQPage',
      inLanguage: 'en',
      mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: f.q,
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
      })),
    },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="BabyName alternative for couples: no ads, no account | Namore"
  description="Looking for an alternative to BabyName – find it together? What BabyName’s own listing says, how Namore differs, and which other baby name apps to consider."
  canonical={canonical}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="post">
    <DisclosureEn />

    <header class="post-head">
      <p class="post-kicker">Alternatives · Retrieved {rival.verified}</p>
      <h1>Looking for a BabyName alternative?</h1>
    </header>

    <p class="post-standfirst">
      BabyName – find it together is the app most couples meet first: 21K ratings, a simple idea,
      swipe and match. If you are here, something about it did not fit. Here is what its own
      listing says, how we do it differently, and which other apps are worth a look.
    </p>

    <h2>Short answer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No ads, no account, and help after the match:</strong> Namore.</li>
      <li><strong>Biggest name pool, community and an AI assistant:</strong> <a href="/blog/namore-vs-baby-name-together">Baby Name Together</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Articles about names alongside swiping:</strong> Nameberry (see <a href="/blog/best-baby-name-apps">all six apps compared</a>).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>BabyName and Namore, side by side</h2>
    <VsTableEn rival={rival} rows={['partner', 'price', 'ads', 'names']} />
    <details class="sf-details">
      <summary>Everything from {rival.name}, word for word</summary>
      <div class="sf-details-inner">
        <StoreFactsEn app={rival} />
      </div>
    </details>

    <Shot
      shots={['welcome', 'shortlist-reveal']}
      alts={['Namore’s invite screen with a six-letter code that connects both phones', 'The reveal in Namore: both rankings combined, favourites at the top']}
      caption="A six-letter code connects both phones, no account. At the end, both rankings combined."
    />

    <h2>What Namore does differently</h2>
    <p>
      The core is the same: you swipe on your own, and a name only appears when you have both said
      yes. What changes is around it. There are no ads, so there is nothing to buy away. There is
      no account; one of you opens a session and the other types a six-letter code. There is one
      price, paid once, that covers both phones, instead of several packs. And after the match
      comes a final round: you each rate your matches 1 to 5 in private, then both rankings are
      shown side by side.
    </p>
    <WhyNamore lang="en" heading="What the app actually does" only={['decision-round', 'shared-deck', 'for-you', 'search-add', 'no-account', 'no-ads', 'privacy-price']} />

    <p class="post-caveat">
      Where BabyName is stronger: it has been around for years and has 21K ratings on the US App
      Store. We have been on the App Store since May 2026 and on Google Play since August 2026. If
      a big user base is what reassures you, that counts for BabyName.
    </p>

    <h2>Other alternatives worth a look</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/blog/namore-vs-baby-name-together">Baby Name Together</a>: 30,000+ names from 40+ countries, AI features, forum and polls, per its listing.</li>
      <li><a href="/blog/best-baby-name-apps">Nameberry, Baby Name Genius, BabyCenter and NameHatch</a>: each quoted from its own listing in our six-app comparison.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-ink" href={APP_STORE_EN(campaign)}>Get Namore for iOS</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={PLAY_EN(campaign)}>Get it on Google Play</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Common questions</h2>
    <dl class="faq">
      {faqs.map((f) => (
        <div class="faq-item">
          <dt>{f.q}</dt>
          <dd>{f.a}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <ClusterFootEn current="babyname-alternative" />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
